.TH fleetring-stop 1  FleetRing "FleetRing manual"
.SH NAME
fleetring\-stop \- Stops a node started in a terminal or a script, after it drains
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfleetring stop\fR [\fB\-\-timeout\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-format\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Stops a node started in a terminal or a script, after it drains
.PP
Sends the node SIGTERM through its process file, which drains it, and waits until it has exited. Refuses a node a supervisor runs. `dev stop` stops the dev node.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
The node\*(Aqs data directory, or a directory holding a `fleetringd.toml`

With a `fleetringd.toml`, its `data_dir` is used: a dev directory and its `data/` both work.
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
The node\*(Aqs configuration file, whose `data_dir` is used
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<TIMEOUT>\fR
How long to wait for the node to drain and exit: `<n>m` or `<n>s`

2m by default. The node keeps draining after that.
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-format\fR \fI<LOG_FORMAT>\fR
Writes log lines as `text` or `json`

Overrides `FLEETRING_LOG_FORMAT` and the configuration file\*(Aqs `[log] format`.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Prints the result and errors only

No progress, notes, warnings or override warnings. A command with no result then prints nothing.
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour log lines and the picker

`auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`; `always` and `never` do as they say.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: On a terminal, unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`
.IP \(bu 2
always: Always, even into a pipe or a file
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
